load @term/seed/code/structure/set
  find set

# A stack machine: a model of computation whose only memory is one or more stacks, evaluating by pushing operands and
# applying operators to the top. It is the execution model of many virtual machines and of postfix notation. With one
# stack it is a pushdown automaton; with two stacks it is as powerful as a Turing machine. The form carries the set of
# stack symbols.
form stack-machine
  link symbols, like set
